    words_note='Five terms for today, and each one gets a picture and a worked number before I lean on it. Pretraining is next-token prediction on a huge collection of text, and it gives a base model. Perplexity is the number engineers quote to show how well pretraining went. Post-training is the two extra steps, supervised fine-tuning and preference tuning such as RLHF. Model families are the main designs you will meet. And a benchmark is a fixed set of questions with an answer key, scored by accuracy. We start where Session 5 ended, with one model and one loss.',
